fields.description:
The organization's own limits. Null is not set: the platform default
applies. Only the organization's administrators read them as set values;
everyone sees the effective ones.

Total is the cycle's total cost (base fee + overage);
Overage is just the part charged against the prepaid
balance.

Error is the robot's most-counted error in the latest bucket;
NoError (or empty) means healthy. Examples: LowBattery,
MobileRobotDelocalized, EStopped.

Token is the opaque bearer value. Shown once, at creation time;
not retrievable afterwards. Pass it in Authorization: Bearer to
authenticate subsequent requests.

ExpiresAt is when the impersonation token stops authenticating;
the frontend shows it in the banner and can route to login as
the deadline approaches.

IsMeaningUsed says the questions were also searched by meaning;
EmbeddingFailureCount is how many could not be embedded and were searched
by words alone.

Permissions is the role's permission set, joined from
role_permission at read time. Output-only on this struct;
SetRolePermissions is the writer.

args.description:
Labels mirror the Docker labels we observed on the image at
upload time. The linker matches on LabelHead + LabelPreset;
the rest are surfaced in the UI.

fields.description:
AssignControllerToOrganization atomically moves a controller to a site
in the requested organization. A changed organization requires siteId;
an empty organization returns it to Launchpad. Requires controller:transfer.

ListChatCandidates lists the people the caller may start a chat with or
add to one. A Mujin user reaches anyone and may name an organization;
anyone else reaches colleagues and the Mujin users they already know.

args.description:
OrganizationID, when non-empty, lists groups in the supplied
org. Cross-organization administrators may pass any org's id;
other callers have it pinned to their own org by the resolver.

OrganizationID, when non-empty, lists roles in the supplied
org. Cross-organization administrators may pass any org's id;
other callers have it pinned to their own org by the resolver.

fields.description:
ListSSHKeys returns the caller's live (non-revoked) SSH keys.
Admin-org members can list any user's keys by setting UserID;
everyone else is restricted to their own.

